course: dictionary
lesson: 14417
title: Too much: the word overly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overly means too much, more than is needed or wanted. It goes in front of a describing word, such as tired, keen or long. «The film was overly long.» The film went on for more time than it should, so it felt too long.
explain: Overly often comes after not, as in «I am not overly keen on spiders.» This is a polite, gentle way of saying you do not like something very much. It sounds calmer than «I hate spiders», because the speaker is holding back. Look for that clue: a careful, quiet tone.
explain: To check the meaning, swap in too much. «The soup was overly salty» becomes «The soup had too much salt», and it still makes sense. If your swap fits the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Overly means too much, more than needed.
fact: Overly is an adverb: it tells you more about an adjective, such as tired or keen.
fact: «Not overly» means not very: «She is not overly tired» means she is only a little tired.
fact: Overly and too are close in meaning, but overly often sounds more careful or formal.
fact: Overly is not the same as over: over can mean above, but overly means too much.
exercise: «The bag was overly heavy, so Sam could not carry it far.» What does overly mean here? | Just the right weight | Empty | Very light | *Too heavy, more than was needed
exercise: «Mia is not overly keen on cold swimming.» What does this tell us? | Mia is angry with the sea | Mia loves it more than anyone | *Mia does not really like it much, and she is being polite | Mia has never been in water
exercise: Which word in «The room was overly hot» tells you the room was too hot? | *overly | room | hot | was
test: Which word means the same as overly? | Very little | Slightly | Never | *Too much
test: «He is not overly fond of loud music.» What does not overly suggest? | He loves it more than anything | *He is not very fond of it, said politely | He has never heard it | He is cross with the music
exam: Ruby says, «The sandwich was overly big for one child.» What does overly big mean? | Just the right size | Hungry | *Too big, more than a child needs | Very small
